{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_1>\ndef solve():\n    n, mod = map(int, input().split())\n    m = n * (n - 1) // 2\n    \n    # Using dictionary-based DP to avoid sparse array allocation\n    dp = [dict() for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    dp1 = [dict() for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    dp[1][m] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Calculate valid range bounds\n        low_bound = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        high_bound = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        \n        for x in range(low_bound, high_bound + 1):\n            if x not in dp[i-1]:\n                continue\n            base_val = dp[i-1][x]\n            for d in range(-i + 1, i):\n                new_val = (dp[i].get(x + d, 0) + base_val * (i - abs(d))) % mod\n                dp[i][x + d] = new_val\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        low_bound = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        high_bound = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        \n        # First loop: multiply previous dp1 by i\n        for x in range(low_bound, high_bound + 1):\n            if x in dp1[i-1]:\n                dp1[i][x] = (dp1[i-1][x] * i) % mod\n        \n        # Second loop: update with dp values\n        for x in range(low_bound, high_bound + 1):\n            if x not in dp[i-1]:\n                continue\n            base_val = dp[i-1][x]\n            for d in range(1, i):\n                new_x = x - d\n                new_val = (dp1[i].get(new_x, 0) + base_val * (i - d)) % mod\n                dp1[i][new_x] = new_val\n\n    # Sum values beyond m\n    result = 0\n    for x in dp1[-1]:\n        if x > m:\n            result = (result + dp1[-1][x]) % mod\n    return result\n\nimport sys\ninput = lambda: sys.stdin.readline().rstrip()\nprint(solve())\n</your_rewritten_code_1>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long solve() {\n    long long n, mod;\n    cin >> n >> mod;\n    long long m = n * (n - 1) / 2;\n    \n    // Using map-based DP to avoid sparse array allocation\n    vector<map<long long, long long>> dp(n + 1);\n    vector<map<long long, long long>> dp1(n + 1);\n    \n    dp[1][m] = 1;\n    \n    for (long long i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n        // Calculate valid range bounds\n        long long low_bound = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n        long long high_bound = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n        \n        for (long long x = low_bound; x <= high_bound; x++) {\n            if (dp[i-1].find(x) == dp[i-1].end()) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            long long base_val = dp[i-1][x];\n            for (long long d = -i + 1; d < i; d++) {\n                long long new_val = (dp[i][x + d] + base_val * (i - abs(d))) % mod;\n                dp[i][x + d] = new_val;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    for (long long i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n        long long low_bound = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n        long long high_bound = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n        \n        // First loop: multiply previous dp1 by i\n        for (long long x = low_bound; x <= high_bound; x++) {\n            if (dp1[i-1].find(x) != dp1[i-1].end()) {\n                dp1[i][x] = (dp1[i-1][x] * i) % mod;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Second loop: update with dp values\n        for (long long x = low_bound; x <= high_bound; x++) {\n            if (dp[i-1].find(x) == dp[i-1].end()) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            long long base_val = dp[i-1][x];\n            for (long long d = 1; d < i; d++) {\n                long long new_x = x - d;\n                long long new_val = (dp1[i][new_x] + base_val * (i - d)) % mod;\n                dp1[i][new_x] = new_val;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Sum values beyond m\n    long long result = 0;\n    for (auto& p : dp1[n]) {\n        if (p.first > m) {\n            result = (result + p.second) % mod;\n        }\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cout << solve() << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.141662692651153e-05, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.0007469248375855386, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0002648479712661356, -4.410734163684538e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.006160674151033163, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.8265450712060556e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.2816193103790283, -0.0004881620698142797, -0.6931713819503784, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.3144184947013855, -4.410734163684538e-06, -0.0032920234370976686, -0.0011174393584951758, 0.0, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.0006301801186054945, -2.0503786799963564e-05, -4.291525328881107e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, -1.728519782773219e-05, -1.6331539882230572e-05, -0.00033778208307921886, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.536738